+Before an upstream response, an accepted upload in `picker-listener.ts` expires after 60 seconds with no body progress. Actual body bytes reset this idle timer, and upstream backpressure pauses it. There is no absolute upload lifetime or additional concurrency cap, so slow uploads can continue as long as they make progress. Body completion, the first upstream response, cancellation and shutdown clear the timer; SSE and long responses do not inherit it. `tests/claude-integration/claude-picker-upload.test.ts` covers silent upstreams, slot recovery, uploads longer than the idle interval and completed/early-response stream preservation. Rejected unfinished uploads close after their empty reply's writable finishes; HTTP/2 uses the
